// Shell plugin — run a command straight from the runner.
//
// Prefix ":sh": typing ":sh systemctl status docker" runs it.
//
// `shell` is set explicitly rather than left as None. With None the plugin reads
// the SHELL environment variable and, if that lookup fails, substitutes the
// literal string "The shell could not be determined!" as the shell name — so a
// command silently becomes a nonsense invocation instead of an error. Observed
// exactly that on this machine: `:sh echo hi` rendered "The shell could not be
// determined!" as its description.
//
// SHELL is set to /usr/bin/zsh in the Hyprland environment (verified via
// /proc/<Hyprland>/environ), so the failure is specific to how the provider
// process inherits its environment, not to the variable being absent session
// wide. Pinning the path here removes the dependency on inheritance entirely.
//
// zsh is the login shell — see dot_zshrc.tmpl and dot_p10k.zsh.

Config(
    prefix: ":sh",
    shell: Some("/usr/bin/zsh"),
)
